{"parentUuid":"bf8666dc-519f-4091-86df-149022ca254e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01R4nZJn72BUk2bc4sK54toh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Got the full schema. Here's the verdict, then I'll save the long-term direction to memory.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- Antigravity docs are an SPA that fetches markdown via `/assets/docs/{path}/{slug}.md` — that's how I bypassed the JS-gated page. Useful trick for future doc spelunking on this site.\n- The schema is closer to Anthropic's Claude Code hooks model (top-level object keyed by **user-given hook names**, each containing event arrays) than to Gemini CLI's (top-level keyed by **event names** directly). That's a meaningful design break from the Gemini CLI heritage.\n- Antigravity only exposes 5 events (PreToolUse / PostToolUse / PreInvocation / PostInvocation / Stop). Entire installs 11 events on Gemini. Several Entire events have no Antigravity equivalent — most importantly **there is no SessionStart in Antigravity**, which is what Entire uses to allocate session state today.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n## Full delta table\n\n| Aspect | Entire on Gemini CLI | Antigravity (authoritative) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Config file | `<repo>/.gemini/settings.json` | `<repo>/.agents/hooks.json` *or* `~/.gemini/config/hooks.json` |\n| Top-level key | event name | **hook name** (user-given), each containing event arrays + optional `enabled` |\n| Events | 11: `SessionStart`, `SessionEnd`, `BeforeAgent`/`AfterAgent`, `BeforeModel`/`AfterModel`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeTool`/`AfterTool`, `PreCompress`, `Notification` | 5: `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `PreInvocation`, `PostInvocation`, `Stop` |\n| Handler fields | `name`, `type`, `command` | `type` (optional, default `\"command\"`), `command`, `timeout` (default 30s) — no `name` |\n| Matcher | per-event | only `PreToolUse`/`PostToolUse`; regex over **Antigravity tool names** (`run_command`, `view_file`, etc.) |\n| Stdin keys | snake_case (Gemini CLI) | **camelCase**: `conversationId`, `workspacePaths`, `transcriptPath`, `artifactDirectoryPath`, `toolCall.{name,args}`, `stepIdx`, `invocationNum`, `terminationReason`, `fullyIdle`, … |\n| Stdout decision | Gemini CLI vocabulary | `decision: allow|deny|ask|force_ask` (PreToolUse), `decision: continue` (Stop), `injectSteps`+`terminationBehavior` (Pre/PostInvocation) |\n\n## Direct answer\n\n**Will Entire's current Gemini hook install work with Antigravity automatically?** No, on three independent counts:\n\n1. **Wrong file & location** — Entire writes `<repo>/.gemini/settings.json`; Antigravity reads `<repo>/.agents/hooks.json` or `~/.gemini/config/hooks.json`. A symlink can't fix this because the shapes also differ.\n2. **Different JSON shape** — Antigravity expects a top-level map keyed by user-given hook *names*, not by event names.\n3. **Different payloads** — `entire hooks gemini <event>` subcommands parse Gemini CLI's snake_case stdin (`session_id`, `cwd`, `tool_name`, etc.). Antigravity sends camelCase keys with different names (`conversationId`, `workspacePaths`, `toolCall.name`). They'd silently fail to parse on every invocation.\n\n## What \"shared config\" actually looks like long-term\n\nNot one file — it's a coordinated pair. Concretely:\n\n- **A new `agent/antigravity/` package** with its own `InstallHooks` writing `.agents/hooks.json` in the right shape.\n- **A new `entire hooks antigravity <event>` subcommand family** (5 events) with its own stdin parser using camelCase fields.\n- **Shared business logic underneath** — both Gemini and Antigravity adapters call the same checkpoint/session strategy, just with different payload shapes feeding it.\n- **Event mapping** Entire needs:\n  - `BeforeTool` → `PreToolUse`; `AfterTool` → `PostToolUse` (1:1)\n  - `BeforeModel` → `PreInvocation`; `AfterModel` → `PostInvocation` (approximate — `PostInvocation` fires after tool calls finish, not after the assistant message)\n  - `SessionStart` → none (lazy-init session state on first event)\n  - `SessionEnd` → `Stop` with `fullyIdle=true`\n  - `PreCompress`, `Notification`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeAgent`/`AfterAgent` → no equivalent; the features that depend on them won't work on Antigravity until Antigravity adds the surface.\n- **Transcript handling**: Antigravity *gives you* `transcriptPath` directly in every payload. Entire's `agent.ResolveSessionFile` resolution dance isn't needed there.\n- **Tool-name matching**: Antigravity uses fixed tool names like `run_command`/`view_file`/`write_to_file`. Entire's \"before-tool\" detect-file-changes logic needs a matcher tuned to Antigravity's vocabulary, not Gemini's.\n\nWhen Gemini CLI deprecates and reroutes, the `gemini-cli` agent entry in `registry.go` can become an alias that redirects to the `antigravity` agent.\n\nSaving the long-term direction so future sessions on this remember it."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6169,"cache_read_input_tokens":151239,"output_tokens":6973,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6169,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":6973,"cache_read_input_tokens":151239,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6169,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6169},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CbCXTrpQCuK8x56HAb1ba","type":"assistant","uuid":"e8229873-5af8-40d3-97aa-dd62573b3ba0","timestamp":"2026-05-19T20:04:33.775Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli","sessionId":"27c10fbd-3055-4d96-8e88-8a95ee2d9e1e","version":"2.1.144","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"e8229873-5af8-40d3-97aa-dd62573b3ba0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01R4nZJn72BUk2bc4sK54toh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VjXjXF2XrQyn5QNqNY6w9Q","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/peytonmontei/.claude/projects/-Users-peytonmontei-Documents-entire-devenv-entireio-cli/memory/project_antigravity_agent_plan.md","content":"---\nname: antigravity-agent-plan\ndescription: Long-term plan to support Antigravity CLI alongside Gemini CLI as a separate agent in the Entire CLI; when Gemini CLI deprecates, alias it to Antigravity. Not started yet — investigation done 2026-05-19.\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nUser wants both Gemini CLI and Antigravity CLI supported as agents long-term, with the eventual plan that when Gemini CLI deprecates, the `gemini-cli` registry entry redirects to `antigravity`. Holding implementation; investigation only as of 2026-05-19.\n\n**Why:** Antigravity 2.0 (launched 2026-05-19) is Google's successor to Gemini CLI. They share the `~/.gemini/` namespace but diverge on hook config shape, file paths, event vocabulary, and stdin payload field names.\n\n**How to apply:** When the user is ready to ship this, the work is roughly:\n\n- New `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/` package implementing `Agent` + `HookSupport`.\n  - `InstallHooks` writes `<repo>/.agents/hooks.json` (workspace) — schema is top-level object keyed by user-given hook *names*, each containing `enabled` (optional) + event arrays (`PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `PreInvocation`, `PostInvocation`, `Stop`). Per-handler fields: `type` (default `\"command\"`), `command`, `timeout` (default 30s). No `name` field on handlers, unlike Gemini.\n  - `AreHooksInstalled` / `UninstallHooks` mirror Gemini's `entireHookPrefixes` approach so the same `entire-` prefix marker still identifies Entire-installed entries.\n  - Five subcommands under `entire hooks antigravity <event>`: `pre-tool-use`, `post-tool-use`, `pre-invocation`, `post-invocation`, `stop`. Each must unmarshal **camelCase** stdin (`conversationId`, `workspacePaths` [array], `transcriptPath`, `artifactDirectoryPath`, `toolCall.{name,args}`, `stepIdx`, `invocationNum`, `terminationReason`, `fullyIdle`, …) — NOT the snake_case Gemini schema.\n- Registry entry in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/registry.go`.\n- Event mapping into Entire's session/checkpoint strategy:\n  - `BeforeTool` ↔ `PreToolUse`, `AfterTool` ↔ `PostToolUse` (1:1)\n  - `BeforeModel` ↔ `PreInvocation`, `AfterModel` ≈ `PostInvocation` (note: PostInvocation fires after tool calls finish, not after assistant message — re-validate before relying on it for \"after-model\" semantics)\n  - `SessionStart` has **no Antigravity equivalent** — lazy-init session state on first event seen\n  - `SessionEnd` ↔ `Stop` with `fullyIdle=true`\n  - `PreCompress`, `Notification`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeAgent`/`AfterAgent` — no equivalent yet; features depending on them won't work on Antigravity until Google adds the surface\n- Antigravity gives `transcriptPath` directly in every payload — no need for the `agent.ResolveSessionFile` resolution dance used for Gemini CLI.\n- Tool-name matcher in `PreToolUse`/`PostToolUse` should target Antigravity's tool vocabulary (`run_command`, `view_file`, `write_to_file`, `replace_file_content`, `multi_replace_file_content`, `list_dir`, `find_by_name`, `grep_search`, `search_web`, `read_url_content`, `run_command`, `manage_task`, `schedule`, `invoke_subagent`, etc.). Use `\"*\"` for \"all tools\" — same idiom as Gemini.\n\nWhen Gemini CLI is officially deprecated, change `geminicli`'s registry entry to alias `antigravity` rather than dropping it (preserves backwards compat for users who have it installed).\n\nSee [[reference-antigravity-docs]] for how to fetch Antigravity docs (SPA blocks WebFetch; fetch `/assets/docs/<path>/<slug>.md` directly).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_se