{"parentUuid":"9262b344-fe98-4842-94e3-2680d2317cb3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01FrH7b7221Us6g2yRqR4NFz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- Claudecode's transcript is JSONL with subagent-file lookups (`agent-<id>.jsonl` in a `subagentsDir`) — see `claudecode/transcript.go:315` — so the plan's \"SubagentAwareExtractor\" intuition matches an existing real pattern.\n- Geminicli's transcript is actually plain **JSON** (not JSONL): `transcript.go:11` says \"Gemini CLI uses JSON format for session storage\", and the top-level is `GeminiTranscript { Messages []GeminiMessage }`. So \"shared with `claudecode` or `geminicli`\" doesn't quite hang together — they're different formats.\n- The existing blank-import pattern in `hooks_cmd.go:12-20` confirms that one line of the plan is correct.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n## Review\n\nThe plan has the right shape but several specifics are **wrong or speculative**, and it's missing a few load-bearing pieces. Going section by section.\n\n### `~/.gemini/config/settings.json` — wrong file name\n\n> *\"verify hooks are written to `~/.gemini/config/settings.json`\"*\n\nThis contradicts the docs we just fetched. The file is **`hooks.json`**, not `settings.json`:\n\n> Hooks are configured in a `hooks.json` file located in your customization directory (e.g., `.agents/` in your workspace or `~/.gemini/config/`).\n\nSo the targets are `<repo>/.agents/hooks.json` (primary) or `~/.gemini/config/hooks.json` (fallback). Writing to `~/.gemini/config/settings.json` would be silently ignored.\n\nAlso: the plan needs to **decide which location to write to**. Workspace `.agents/hooks.json` is the natural pick (matches Entire's current `<repo>/.gemini/settings.json` convention — it's per-repo). But this should be explicit, not implicit.\n\n### `~/.gemini/tmp/` transcript discovery — likely wrong, and not needed\n\n> *\"Session Discovery: Look in `~/.gemini/tmp/` for transcripts (likely JSONL format).\"*\n\nTwo problems:\n\n1. **Wrong location.** `~/.gemini/tmp/` is the existing Gemini CLI convention (`geminicli/gemini.go:112`). The Antigravity docs' own example shows transcripts at `<workspace>/.gemini/jetski/transcript.jsonl` — workspace-relative, in a `jetski` subdir (runtime code name), not the user home.\n2. **Discovery isn't needed at all.** Every Antigravity hook payload includes `transcriptPath` directly in stdin (along with `artifactDirectoryPath`). We don't have to guess where transcripts live — Antigravity hands us the path on every event. That makes `GetSessionDir`-style resolution dead weight here.\n\nAlso \"likely JSONL\" is a speculation. The doc example literally calls the file `transcript.jsonl`, so it's confirmed JSONL; just say so.\n\n### \"Shared with `claudecode` or new\" JSONL parsing — verify before sharing\n\nAntigravity supports multiple model providers (Gemini, Claude, GPT). The on-disk transcript schema is *not specified* anywhere in the hooks doc — only the stdin/stdout contract is. Two real possibilities:\n\n- It's Anthropic-format JSONL (claudecode-shareable) when the user runs Antigravity on Claude.\n- It's a Google-internal format (jetski's own schema) regardless of model.\n\n**Don't commit to \"shared with claudecode\" until you've inspected an actual `transcript.jsonl` sample.** Fetch one by running Antigravity once and reading the file at the `transcriptPath` it emits. Plan a verification step before plan acceptance.\n\n### \"Subagent\" tracking — partially valid\n\nAntigravity does have subagents — the tools `invoke_subagent`, `define_subagent`, `manage_subagents`, and a `Subagents` array argument with per-subagent `Workspace`. So a `SubagentAwareExtractor` is conceptually justified. But how subagent transcripts are persisted is undocumented; this is another \"verify before building\" item.\n\n### Hooks_cmd.go blank import — correct\n\nConfirmed against `hooks_cmd.go:12-20`. Pattern matches.\n\n## Load-bearing gaps the plan is missing\n\nListed roughly by severity:\n\n1. **No `SessionStart` event in Antigravity.** Only 5 events exist (PreToolUse, PostToolUse, PreInvocation, PostInvocation, Stop). Entire currently allocates session state in `entire hooks gemini session-start`. The plan **must** lazy-init session state on the first event seen — most likely the first `PreInvocation` — and key it by Antigravity's `conversationId` (UUID). Without this, `entire status` will show nothing.\n\n2. **Stdin payload is camelCase with different field names.** Examples:\n\n   | Gemini CLI (snake_case) | Antigravity (camelCase) |\n   |---|---|\n   | `session_id` | `conversationId` |\n   | `cwd` (scalar) | `workspacePaths` (array) |\n   | `tool_name` | `toolCall.name` |\n   | `tool_input` | `toolCall.args` |\n   | (resolved via `ResolveSessionFile`) | `transcriptPath` (given) |\n\n   The plan needs its own struct types for unmarshaling. \"Reuse Gemini hook parsers\" will silently produce zero-valued structs.\n\n3. **Multi-workspace handling.** `workspacePaths` is an array. Entire's worktree resolution assumes a single CWD. The plan should specify which workspace becomes the session's \"repo root\" (probably index 0, but state this explicitly).\n\n4. **`Stop` with `fullyIdle=false`.** Stop fires when execution terminates *but background commands may still be running*. The plan needs to not tear down session state when `fullyIdle=false`; treat it like an idle transition instead.\n\n5. **Tool-name vocabulary.** `BeforeTool`'s file-change detection in Entire is tuned to Gemini's tool names. Antigravity's mutating tools are `write_to_file`, `replace_file_content`, `multi_replace_file_content`, `run_command`. The matcher regex (`\"write_to_file|replace_file_content|multi_replace_file_content\"` etc., or just `\"*\"`) needs to be authored for Antigravity, not borrowed.\n\n6. **Event coverage drops.** Features tied to `PreCompress`, `Notification`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeAgent`/`AfterAgent`, `BeforeModel` (≠ `PreInvocation` precisely), `SessionEnd` (logout) will not have parity. The plan should either state these gaps explicitly or scope the agent as \"compaction-aware, notifications: no\" up front.\n\n7. **No verification step for the stdin parser.** Test plan jumps from `go test` to \"start an Antigravity session.\" There should be an interim **fixture test** that feeds known Antigravity stdin JSON payloads (lifted verbatim from the doc examples) into the new `entire hooks antigravity <event>` subcommands and asserts they parse without error. Cheap, deterministic, catches the camelCase mistakes.\n\n8. **No mention of `entire review`.** Geminicli has a `reviewer.go` for `entire review`. If Antigravity is to be a peer agent, that surface needs equivalent support (or be explicitly out of scope for v1).\n\n## Recommended revisions before acceptance\n\n1. Change config target to `<repo>/.agents/hooks.json` (and document why — workspace-scoped, matches Entire's existing per-repo settings convention).\n2. Delete the \"Session Discovery\" task; replace with \"Use `transcriptPath` from every payload directly.\"\n3. Replace \"shared with `claudecode` or new\" with a concrete verification step: \"Run Antigravity once, inspect `transcript.jsonl`, then decide parser strategy.\"\n4. Add a \"Lazy session init on first `PreInvocation`, keyed by `conversationId`\" task.\n5. Add fixture tests using the four stdin example payloads from the docs (PreToolUse, PostToolUse, PreInvocation, Stop).\n6. Add an explicit \"Feature parity\" table calling out which Entire features will not work on Antigravity v1 (PreCompress, Notification, before-tool-selection, granular session-start/end).\n7. Manual verification step: change `~/.gemini/config/settings.json` → `<repo>/.agents/hooks.json`.\n\nWant me to draft a revised plan, or pass these notes to a `Plan` agent for a rewrite?"}],"stop_reason