er\n- If Gemini-style messages → adapt geminicli parser\n- If novel jetski-internal shape → write fresh parser\n\n**Do not proceed to Task 2 until this fixture exists and the decision is recorded.**\n\n### Task 2: Agent skeleton + interface assertion\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/agent.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/agent_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/agent_test.go\npackage antigravity\n\nimport (\n    \"testing\"\n\n    \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n)\n\nfunc TestAgent_Name(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    a := &AntigravityAgent{}\n    if a.Name() != \"antigravity\" {\n        t.Errorf(\"Name() = %q, want %q\", a.Name(), \"antigravity\")\n    }\n}\n\nfunc TestAgent_ImplementsAgent(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    var _ agent.Agent = (*AntigravityAgent)(nil)\n    var _ agent.HookSupport = (*AntigravityAgent)(nil)\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n\n```\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/ -run TestAgent -v\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL with `undefined: AntigravityAgent`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement minimal agent**\n\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/agent.go\npackage antigravity\n\nimport \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n\nconst AgentName = \"antigravity\"\n\n// AntigravityAgent implements the Agent and HookSupport interfaces for\n// Google Antigravity CLI (successor to Gemini CLI as of 2026-05).\ntype AntigravityAgent struct{}\n\nfunc (a *AntigravityAgent) Name() string             { return AgentName }\nfunc (a *AntigravityAgent) AgentType() agent.AgentType { return agent.AgentTypeAntigravity }\nfunc (a *AntigravityAgent) IsPreview() bool           { return true } // remove after stabilization\n```\n\nThen add the constant to `cmd/entire/cli/agent/types.go` (or wherever `AgentType` lives — check first):\n\n```fish\ngrep -n \"AgentTypeGeminiCLI\\|AgentTypeClaudeCode\" cmd/entire/cli/agent/types/*.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/types.go 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nAdd `AgentTypeAntigravity` alongside the existing constants in the same file.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Verify it builds and tests pass**\n\n```\ngo build ./... && go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/ -run TestAgent -v\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n### Task 3: Hook config types + stdin/stdout types\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/types.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/types_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/testdata/hook_stdin_*.json` (5 files, verbatim from docs)\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Copy the five docs examples into testdata/**\n\nThese are the exact JSON payloads from the Antigravity hooks doc we fetched. Each goes in its own file. (PreToolUse example shown; the other four are in the docs and were captured in conversation memory.)\n\n```json\n// testdata/hook_stdin_pretooluse.json\n{\n  \"toolCall\": {\n    \"name\": \"run_command\",\n    \"args\": {\n      \"CommandLine\": \"npm test\",\n      \"Cwd\": \"/workspace/project\",\n      \"WaitMsBeforeAsync\": 5000\n    }\n  },\n  \"stepIdx\": 19,\n  \"conversationId\": \"ec33ebf9-0cba-4100-8142-c61503f6c587\",\n  \"workspacePaths\": [\"/workspace/project\"],\n  \"transcriptPath\": \"/workspace/project/.gemini/jetski/transcript.jsonl\",\n  \"artifactDirectoryPath\": \"/workspace/project/.gemini/jetski/artifacts\"\n}\n```\n\nRepeat for `posttooluse`, `preinvocation`, `postinvocation`, `stop`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write failing round-trip tests**\n\n```go\n// types_test.go\npackage antigravity\n\nimport (\n    \"encoding/json\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"path/filepath\"\n    \"testing\"\n)\n\nfunc TestParse_PreToolUse_Fixture(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    data, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"testdata\", \"hook_stdin_pretooluse.json\"))\n    if err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n    var p PreToolUsePayload\n    if err := json.Unmarshal(data, &p); err != nil { t.Fatalf(\"unmarshal: %v\",