{"parentUuid":"5860d166-f379-4f19-8b23-4646ad7de02d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DULXTHafaPz3roKWV5jqDB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019DehqLjuWvYwRcEXkd1EQF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/antigravity-plan-for-review.md","content":"# Antigravity Agent Integration Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Add Antigravity CLI as a first-class agent in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/`, peer to `geminicli`, with hook config, lifecycle handlers, and session tracking.\n\n**Architecture:** New agent package implementing `Agent` + `HookSupport`. Writes `<repo>/.agents/hooks.json` (Antigravity's distinct file, NOT `.gemini/settings.json`). Five lifecycle subcommands (`entire hooks antigravity {pre-tool-use,post-tool-use,pre-invocation,post-invocation,stop}`) parse **camelCase** stdin payloads — a separate parser from Gemini's snake_case schema. Session state lazy-inits on first `PreInvocation` keyed by `conversationId` (Antigravity has no SessionStart event). Transcript path is read directly from each payload's `transcriptPath` field (no discovery dance).\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x, cobra, go-git, existing `agent.HookSupport` interface, `IsManagedHookCommand` for ownership marking, `manualcommit` strategy via `session.StateStore`.\n\n**Phasing:**\n- **v1 (this plan):** Install/uninstall hooks; capture all 5 events; lazy session init; record file changes from `PreToolUse`/`PostToolUse`; condense on `Stop` when `fullyIdle=true`. Transcript schema verified once before parser commitment.\n- **Deferred (separate plans):** `entire review` reviewer for Antigravity (mirror `geminicli/reviewer.go`); subagent transcript tracking; `entire status` token usage; alias `gemini-cli` → `antigravity` when Google deprecates Gemini CLI.\n\n**Commit strategy:** 3 logical commits at chunk boundaries (per memory: \"Few commits per PR\").\n\n---\n\n## File Structure\n\n**New files** (all under `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/`):\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `agent.go` | `AntigravityAgent` struct, `Name()`, `AgentType()`, `IsPreview()` |\n| `agent_test.go` | Construction + interface assertion tests |\n| `types.go` | `HooksFile`, `HookConfig`, `HookHandler`, `EventMatcher` (config); `PreToolUsePayload`, etc. (stdin); decision/output types (stdout) — all camelCase JSON tags |\n| `types_test.go` | Round-trip JSON marshal tests against `testdata/` fixtures |\n| `hooks.go` | `InstallHooks`/`UninstallHooks`/`AreHooksInstalled` writing `<repo>/.agents/hooks.json` |\n| `hooks_test.go` | Idempotency, force re-install, partial-existing-file preservation |\n| `hook_command.go` | Cobra subcommand registration for `entire hooks antigravity <event>` (5 verbs) |\n| `lifecycle.go` | Stdin parsers + lazy session-state init keyed by `conversationId`; per-event handler bodies |\n| `lifecycle_test.go` | Lazy init, multi-event flow, `fullyIdle=false` does not finalize, file-change extraction from `PreToolUse`/`PostToolUse` |\n| `transcript.go` | JSONL reader — body deferred to Chunk 1 Task 1 (verify schema first) |\n| `transcript_test.go` | Schema parse tests against captured fixture |\n| `registry.go` | `init()` that calls `agent.Register(...)` |\n| `testdata/hook_stdin_pretooluse.json` | Verbatim from Antigravity docs example |\n| `testdata/hook_stdin_posttooluse.json` | Verbatim from docs |\n| `testdata/hook_stdin_preinvocation.json` | Verbatim from docs |\n| `testdata/hook_stdin_postinvocation.json` | Verbatim from docs |\n| `testdata/hook_stdin_stop.json` | Verbatim from docs |\n| `testdata/transcript_sample.jsonl` | **Captured live** in Chunk 1 Task 1 |\n\n**Modified files:**\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_cmd.go` | Add `_ \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity\"` blank import (after geminicli line) |\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 1: Recon and Foundation\n\nThis chunk is **gated** on a one-time real-world capture step. Do not skip Task 1 — it determines whether the transcript parser shares with `claudecode` or needs its own schema. After Task 1, Tasks 2–4 are pure code.\n\n### Task 1: Capture a real Antigravity transcript fixture\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/testdata/transcript_sample.jsonl`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Install Antigravity CLI locally**\n\nSuggest the user run (interactive — they need to type it):\n\n```fish\n! npm install -g @antigravity/cli\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run a minimal Antigravity session in a throwaway repo**\n\n```fish\nmkdir -p /tmp/ag-fixture-repo && cd /tmp/ag-fixture-repo && git init -q\necho \"hello\" > a.txt && git add . && git commit -m init -q\nantigravity --prompt \"read a.txt and tell me what it says, then exit\"\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Locate and copy the transcript**\n\n```fish\nset ts /tmp/ag-fixture-repo/.gemini/jetski/transcript.jsonl\ntest -f $ts; and cp $ts /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/testdata/transcript_sample.jsonl\n```\n\nExpected: file exists; ~10–50 JSONL lines.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Inspect schema and decide parser strategy**\n\n```fish\nhead -3 cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/testdata/transcript_sample.jsonl | jq .\n```\n\nCompare to `claudecode/transcript.go` JSONL shape and `geminicli/transcript.go` JSON shape. Record decision (in a code comment in the eventual `transcript.go`):\n- If Anthropic message-block shape → import claudecode parser\n- If Gemini-style messages → adapt geminicli parser\n- If novel jetski-internal shape → write fresh parser\n\n**Do not proceed to Task 2 until this fixture exists and the decision is recorded.**\n\n### Task 2: Agent skeleton + interface assertion\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/agent.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/agent_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**\n\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/agent_test.go\npackage antigravity\n\nimport (\n    \"testing\"\n\n    \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n)\n\nfunc TestAgent_Name(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    a := &AntigravityAgent{}\n    if a.Name() != \"antigravity\" {\n        t.Errorf(\"Name() = %q, want %q\", a.Name(), \"antigravity\")\n    }\n}\n\nfunc TestAgent_ImplementsAgent(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    var _ agent.Agent = (*AntigravityAgent)(nil)\n    var _ agent.HookSupport = (*AntigravityAgent)(nil)\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**\n\n```\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/ -run TestAgent -v\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL with `undefined: AntigravityAgent`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement minimal agent**\n\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/agent.go\npackage antigravity\n\nimport \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n\nconst AgentName = \"antigravity\"\n\n// AntigravityAgent implements the Agent and HookSupport interfaces for\n// Google Antigravity CLI (successor to Gemini CLI as of 2026-05).\ntype AntigravityAgent struct{}\n\nfunc (a *AntigravityAgent) Name() string             { return AgentName }\nfunc (a *AntigravityAgent) AgentType() agent.AgentType { return agent.AgentTypeAntigravity }\nfunc (a *AntigravityAgent) IsPreview() bool           { return true } // remove after stabilization\n```\n\nThen add the constant to `cmd/entire/cli/agent/types.go` (or wherever `AgentType` lives — check first):\n\n```fish\ngrep -n \"AgentTypeGeminiCLI\\|AgentTypeClaudeCode\" cmd/entire/cli/agent/types/*.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/types.go 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nAdd `AgentTypeAntigravity` alongside the existing constants in the same file.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Verify it builds and tests pass**\n\n```\ngo build ./... && go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/ -run TestAgent -v\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n### Task 3: Hook config types + stdin/stdout types\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/types.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/types_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/testdata/hook_stdin_*.json` (5 files, verbatim from docs)\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Copy the five docs examples into testdata/**\n\nThese are the exact JSON payloads from the Antigravity hooks doc we fetched. Each goes in its own file. (PreToolUse example shown; the other four are in the docs and were captured in conversation memory.)\n\n```json\n// testdata/hook_stdin_pretooluse.json\n{\n  \"toolCall\": {\n    \"name\": \"run_command\",\n    \"args\": {\n      \"CommandLine\": \"npm test\",\n      \"Cwd\": \"/workspace/project\",\n      \"WaitMsBeforeAsync\": 5000\n    }\n  },\n  \"stepIdx\": 19,\n  \"conversationId\": \"ec33ebf9-0cba-4100-8142-c61503f6c587\",\n  \"workspacePaths\": [\"/workspace/project\"],\n  \"transcriptPath\": \"/workspace/project/.gemini/jetski/transcript.jsonl\",\n  \"artifactDirectoryPath\": \"/workspace/project/.gemini/jetski/artifacts\"\n}\n```\n\nRepeat for `posttooluse`, `preinvocation`, `postinvocation`, `stop`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write failing round-trip tests**\n\n```go\n// types_test.go\npackage antigravity\n\nimport (\n    \"encoding/json\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"path/filepath\"\n    \"testing\"\n)\n\nfunc TestParse_PreToolUse_Fixture(t *testing.T) {\n    t.Parallel()\n    data, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"testdata\", \"hook_stdin_pretooluse.json\"))\n    if err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n    var p PreToolUsePayload\n    if err := json.Unmarshal(data, &p); err != nil { t.Fatalf(\"unmarshal: %v\", err) }\n    if p.ConversationID != \"ec33ebf9-0cba-4100-8142-c61503f6c587\" {\n        t.Errorf(\"conversationId = %q\", p.ConversationID)\n    }\n    if p.ToolCall.Name != \"run_command\" {\n        t.Errorf(\"toolCall.name = %q\", p.ToolCall.Name)\n    }\n    if len(p.WorkspacePaths) != 1 || p.WorkspacePaths[