- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/lifecycle.go`\n602\t- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/lifecycle_test.go`\n603\t\n604\tThe contract here (per `agent.go:88-104`) is `HookNames() []string` + `ParseHookEvent(ctx, hookName, stdin) (*Event, error)`. We do NOT define standalone `HandleX` functions — the framework drives the subcommand dispatch and calls `ParseHookEvent`. We return a normalized `agent.Event` (or `nil` for hooks with no lifecycle significance).\n605\t\n606\t**Event mapping (Antigravity → Entire):**\n607\t\n608\t| Antigravity hook | Returned `Event.Type` |\n609\t|---|---|\n610\t| `pre-invocation` | `agent.TurnStart` (always — the framework's TurnStart handler calls `strategy.InitializeSession` at `cli/lifecycle.go:406`, which is idempotent; first arrival creates state, subsequent arrivals reuse it) |\n611\t| `post-invocation` | `agent.TurnEnd` |\n612\t| `stop` (fullyIdle=true) | `agent.SessionEnd` |\n613\t| `stop` (fullyIdle=false) | `nil` (background tasks still running) |\n614\t| `pre-tool-use` | `agent.ToolUse` with extracted `ModifiedFiles`/`NewFiles` for `write_to_file`/`replace_file_content`/`multi_replace_file_content`; `nil` for non-mutating tools |\n615\t| `post-tool-use` | `nil` (PreToolUse already captured file impact) |\n616\t\n617\t**Decision: no explicit SessionStart event in v1.** Antigravity has no SessionStart hook surface. The natural map would be \"first PreInvocation → SessionStart, then later TurnStart on the next one\" — but the *first turn's* tool events arrive **between** PreInvocation #1 and PreInvocation #2, before session state would exist. Rather than fire two events from one hook (which `ParseHookEvent`'s `(*Event, error)` contract does not allow), v1 always returns `TurnStart` from PreInvocation. The cost: the SessionStart-only side effects (banner from `handleLifecycleSessionStart` at `cli/lifecycle.go:98-205`) never fire for Antigravity. Document this gap in the Deferred table; a follow-up can fire SessionStart inline before returning TurnStart on first-ever invocation once we confirm the framework tolerates that ordering.\n618\t\n619\tHook constants:\n620\t\n621\t```go\n622\tconst (\n623\t    HookNamePreToolUse     = \"pre-tool-use\"\n624\t    HookNamePostToolUse    = \"post-tool-use\"\n625\t    HookNamePreInvocation  = \"pre-invocation\"\n626\t    HookNamePostInvocation = \"post-invocation\"\n627\t    HookNameStop           = \"stop\"\n628\t)\n629\t```\n630\t\n631\t- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing tests**\n632\t\n633\t```go\n634\t// lifecycle_test.go\n635\tpackage antigravity\n636\t\n637\timport (\n638\t    \"bytes\"\n639\t    \"context\"\n640\t    \"os\"\n641\t    \"path/filepath\"\n642\t    \"strings\"\n643\t    \"testing\"\n644\t\n645\t    \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n646\t    \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/testutil\"\n647\t)\n648\t\n649\tfunc TestHookNames(t *testing.T) {\n650\t    t.Parallel()\n651\t    a := &AntigravityAgent{}\n652\t    names := a.HookNames()\n653\t    want := []string{\"pre-tool-use\", \"post-tool-use\", \"pre-invocation\", \"post-invocation\", \"stop\"}\n654\t    if len(names) != len(want) { t.Fatalf(\"got %d, want %d\", len(names), len(want)) }\n655\t    // ... iterate to compare\n656\t}\n657\t\n658\tfunc TestParseHookEvent_PreInvocationEmitsTurnStart(t *testing.T) {\n659\t    t.Parallel()\n660\t    data, _ := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"testdata\", \"hook_stdin_preinvocation.json\"))\n661\t    a := &AntigravityAgent{}\n662\t    ev, err := a.ParseHookEvent(context.Background(), HookNamePreInvocation, bytes.NewReader(data))\n663\t    if err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n664\t    if ev == nil || ev.Type != agent.TurnStart {\n665\t        t.Errorf(\"got %v, want TurnStart\", ev)\n666\t    }\n667\t    if ev.SessionID != \"ec33ebf9-0cba-4100-8142-c61503f6c587\" {\n668\t        t.Errorf(\"SessionID = %q\", ev.SessionID)\n669\t    }\n670\t    if !strings.HasSuffix(ev.SessionRef, \"transcript.jsonl\") {\n671\t        t.Error