{"parentUuid":"86371f6d-ec42-4295-bcf7-1a985d058399","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01UKeWN915PhMCxUoNPLyYr2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## To answer the strategic question directly\n\n**We are sharing — at the framework helper level, not at the file level.** That's how the architecture works.\n\nThe `agent` package (`cmd/entire/cli/agent/`) exposes these shared helpers that every agent uses:\n\n| Shared helper | What Antigravity uses it for |\n|---|---|\n| `agent.ChunkJSONL` / `agent.ReassembleJSONL` | Transcript chunking (`chunking.go:73,109`) |\n| `agent.ChunkTranscript` / `agent.ReassembleTranscript` | High-level dispatch by agent type (`chunking.go:24,47`) |\n| `agent.WrapProductionSilentHookCommand` | Wrapping hook commands for production (`hook_command.go:30`) |\n| `agent.IsManagedHookCommand` | Ownership detection in foreign-hook scenarios (`hook_command.go:71`) |\n| `agent.RunIsolatedTextGeneratorCLI` | Running `antigravity -p \"<prompt>\"` for summaries (`text_generator_cli.go:21`) |\n| `agent.IsSummaryCLIAvailable` | Detecting if antigravity is on PATH (`text_generator_cli.go:86`) |\n\nThese are exactly what `geminicli` uses today. Antigravity calls into the same helpers from its own per-agent files.\n\n**What can't be shared at the file level** with geminicli:\n\n| Per-agent code | Why net-new for Antigravity |\n|---|---|\n| `hooks.go` (install) | File path `.agents/hooks.json` vs `.gemini/settings.json`; top-level keyed by **hook-name** vs **event-name** |\n| `lifecycle.go` (ParseHookEvent) | 5 events vs 11; different stdin payload schema (camelCase vs snake_case) |\n| `types.go` (payload structs) | camelCase JSON tags + different field names (`conversationId` vs `session_id`, `workspacePaths` array vs `cwd` scalar, `toolCall.{name,args}` vs `tool_name`/`tool_input`) |\n\nYou literally cannot have one file serve both wire formats — they're different protocols that happen to share a heritage. This is the same reason `claudecode` and `codex` have separate `hooks.go` files even though both write JSON config.\n\n**What MIGHT share** with geminicli: the transcript parser, IF Antigravity's on-disk JSONL schema turns out to overlap with Gemini's. That's why my plan defers the parser body to Chunk 3 Task 9 — capture a real fixture first, then decide.\n\n## And the file-layout gaps I should fix\n\nThe canonical guide at `docs/architecture/agent-guide.md` confirms the file layout:\n\n```\ncmd/entire/cli/agent/antigravity/\n├── antigravity.go    # Core Agent impl + init()       ← I had this\n├── lifecycle.go      # ParseHookEvent                 ← I had this\n├── types.go          # Hook input structs            ← I had this\n├── hooks.go          # HookSupport impl              ← I had this\n├── transcript.go     # Transcript methods           ← I INLINED into antigravity.go — wrong\n└── (tests for each)\n```\n\nPlus the optional but conventional additions:\n- `generate.go` — `GenerateText` for summary provider (5/8 agents have it)\n- `discovery.go` — `DiscoverReviewSkills` stub (3/8 agents; geminicli stubs with `return nil, nil`)\n\nThe fix is small: 3 file moves/additions, mostly stubs."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3876,"cache_read_input_tokens":330013,"output_tokens":2459,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3876,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2459,"cache_read_input_tokens":330013,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3876},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CbEQRR2kXiEQTmuSZ3hpW","type":"assistant","uuid":"d68b347d-60a7-40c0-b610-789a3837aef8","timestamp":"2026-05-20T